 "equipment_type": "Indirect gas-fired heating and make-up air unit controller",
 "applies_to": "Modine indirect gas-fired heating and make-up air units, model series D, H, I and O, with the Modine Controls System (Carel pCOOEM+ medium controller).",
 "summary": "Modine's indirect gas-fired heating and make-up air units use a Carel pCOOEM+ controller; with a BMS interface card it talks BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP/Ethernet (LonWorks is the other option). The BMS can switch the unit on and off, send occupancy, reset alarms, send a heartbeat and write space, supply-air, neutral-air, dewpoint, humidity, CO2, damper and fan-speed setpoints. It reads temperatures, dewpoints, enthalpies, humidities, pressures, demands, digital inputs, relay outputs and a long list of individual alarm flags.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Carel analog variables are AV 1-51, Carel integer variables are AV 1001-1084 and digital variables are BV 1-81.",
  "Unit_Status, Occupancy_Status, Unit_Mode and Mechanical_Temp_Lockouts return codes; the table refers to the controls manual for the values.",
  "For AV 30-36 the description column prints only a default and range (e.g. '55F (0-100)').",
  "BV 39 (Dout_DX_CW_Stage_2) and BV 40 (Dout_Evap_Cool_Pump) are printed with each other's descriptions; they are shown as printed.",
  "BV 80-81 (A2L leak alarm and mitigation) apply to units with A2L refrigerant.",
  "Engineering units are not printed in the table. Source table 'Typical BMS System Variables', manual pages 51-54 (175 objects)."
 ],
